\section{Image Fusion}\label{app:imagefusion}

Each damage image undergoes preprocessing to remove a fixed background color and isolate damage features with an alpha channel. Subsequently, we generate complex masks to give natural shapes to the damage artifacts. These masks, randomly shaped as clouds, slender stripes, or irregular ellipses, are created using operations like noise addition, Gaussian blurring, and morphological transformations.

The damage patches are resized proportionally to the tombstone images and blended through per-pixel alpha blending, controlling transparency within a predefined range for subtle integration. Multiple overlays with varied scaling and blending weights produce augmented images that effectively simulate realistic deterioration. 

