Note that the fixed centers of the LOLIMOT-partitioned state space make this effect visible. It can hardly be investigated for deep neural state space models or recurrent neural networks, where all neural weights are trainable parameters. Furthermore, it must be mentioned that the observed behavior (Fig.~\ref{fig:xTraj}) enables modeling with low flexibility. In the case of LMSSN this means that only one split is sufficient for the complete identification. Thus it is very effective because only two local \textit{linear} models are able to fit a process with a smooth curve~\eqref{eq:process}.

