\begin{lemma}
    The morphism $\phi$ satisfies $2\phi = s^t$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
    We know that $2\phi \circ s =2\phi\circ 2\psi = 4\text{Id}=s^t\circ s.$ Since $s$ is surjective, hence an epimorphism, we have that $2\phi = s^t$.
\end{proof}

