Let $p_l$ and $p_r$ be the unique, lowest degree polynomials such that $p_l$ interpolates $\{(x_j,f_j)\}_{j=1}^d$ and $p_r$ interpolates $\{(x_j,f_j)\}_{j=N-d+1}^N$. Define the extension 
$\{\tilde{f}_j\}$ as follows
$$
    \tilde{f}_j = \begin{cases}
        p_l(x_j), &\text{ if } j<1,\\
        f_j, &\text{ if } 1\le j\le N,\\
        p_r(x_j), & \text{ if } j>N.
    \end{cases}
