\noindent The first electrode was positioned \(0.1 \, \text{cm}\) away from the mesh in the y-direction, at the midpoint along both the x- and z-axes. The second electrode was placed at the same x- and z-coordinate but was directly on the tissue mesh. Figure \ref{fig:benchmark_results} displays the recovered ECG traces from this benchmark simulation. The simulation was run for a duration of 300 ms, with an ODE timestep of 0.03125 ms. The region around the electrode activated at approximately the same time as the peak seen in the ECG matching expected behavior (see Figure \ref{fig:activation_map_benchmark}). The overall pattern of the recovered traces aligns with the expected results and are consistent with similar previously conducted simulations \citeS{ecg_eq_1}.

