Considering data freshness as a key requirement for flight safety, the communication delay during data packet transmission must be constrained within a reasonable range to avoid potential collision risks. Therefore, in this work, we aim to derive a probabilistic delay bound, $P\{D > T\}$, defined as the probability that the packet delay $D$ exceeds a given threshold $T$, based on the Stochastic Network Calculus theory.

