We call this choice of frame the $\one$-frame.

The three-body interaction terms in \eqref{eq:spinham} make it so that $\Delta \neq 0$.
Therefore, if we apply the optimization procedure described in Section \ref{sec:subsystem},
we would expect to find a decomposition that better separates the logical subsystem from the environment.
Here we have chosen the regularization hyperparameter to be $\eta = 0.01$.
