%In the language of machine learning, \gls{tmd} provides an unsupervised, analytical analogue of an autoencoder, in which the "latent space" corresponds to the spectrum of topological modes. This spectrum is fully determined by the Laplacian of the interaction graph, and it defines a natural hierarchy of spatial features. Low-energy Chladni states encode global modes, while higher-energy ones capture finer, local fluctuations. In this framework, memory, pattern recognition, and metastability emerge as natural consequences of the topological structure—rather than being trained through data.
