For $k\geqslant 7$, there are a lot of Hilbert strata not contained in the smoothable component corresponding to 2-step ideals with few syzygies (see \Cref{fig:newA3k7-8}). In those cases, we apply \Cref{thm: homo loco syz} and compute explicitly the dimension of the generic fibre of $\psi_{\bh}$. See the ancillary \textit{Macaulay2} file \href{www.paololella.it/software/reducibility-Hilbert-schemes.m2}{\tt reducibility-Hilbert-schemes.m2} to produce and check the list of Hilbert strata not contained in the smoothable component.


